# VoiceScript — Setup Guide

## ⚡ Quickest way to run it (30 seconds)

Chrome blocks the microphone on `http://localhost` (Live Server).
**Do NOT use Live Server.** Instead:

### Option 1 — Open directly in Chrome (easiest, zero setup)
1. In VS Code, right-click `index.html` in the Explorer sidebar
2. Click **"Reveal in File Explorer"** (Windows) or **"Reveal in Finder"** (Mac)
3. Double-click `index.html` — it opens in your default browser
4. Or drag it straight into a Chrome window

That's it. Chrome allows mic on `file://` pages. It will work immediately.

---

### Option 2 — Proper HTTPS local server via Node

Run this once in your VS Code terminal:

```bash
npx serve . --ssl-cert /path/to/cert.pem
```

Or the simplest HTTPS dev server:

```bash
npx http-server . -S -C cert.pem -K key.pem
```

---

### Option 3 — Allow mic on localhost in Chrome flags

1. Open Chrome and go to: `chrome://flags/#unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure`
2. Add `http://127.0.0.1:5500` (or whatever port Live Server uses)
3. Set it to **Enabled**
4. Relaunch Chrome
5. Now Live Server will work fine with the mic

---

